njured reserve after he underwent shoulder surgery.","published":"2025-08-08T00:24:20.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/45921884/lions-cb-ennis-rakestraw-placed-season-ending-ir","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Eric Woodyard","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Source: Lions RB Jahmyr Gibbs injures hamstring at practice","description":"Lions running back Jahmyr Gibbs suffered a hamstring injury at practice Monday night, a source told ESPN's Adam Schefter.","published":"2024-08-13T03:27:12.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/40840173/detroit-lions-running-back-jahmyr-gibbs-injures-hamstring-practice","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Eric Woodyard","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Detroit Lions 2024 NFL draft picks: Selection analysis","description":"Let's take a closer look at each of the Lions' 2024 draft picks.","published":"2024-04-27T23:42:55.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/draft2024/story/_/id/39962918/detroit-lions-nfl-draft-picks-2024-selection-analysis-depth-chart","type":"Story","byline":"Eric Woodyard","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Mizzou's Ennis Rakestraw, Ty'Ron Hopper out vs. OSU, source says","description":"Missouri cornerback Ennis Rakestraw Jr. and linebacker Ty'Ron Hopper will not play in the Goodyear Cotton Bowl Classic against Ohio State, a source told ESPN.","published":"2023-12-23T19:02:48.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/39173568/mizzou-ennis-rakestraw-tyron-hopper-vs-osu-source-says","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Missouri Tigers CB Ennis Rakestraw Jr. tears ACL in practice","description":"Missouri cornerback Ennis Rakestraw Jr. suffered a torn ACL in practice Tuesday.","published":"2021-10-06T17:08:29.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/32348638/missouri-tigers-cb-ennis-rakestraw-jr-tears-acl-practice","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"}],"wiki":{"title":"Ennis Rakestraw Jr.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ennis_Rakestraw_Jr.","description":"American football player (born 2002)","touched":"2026-11-22T23:50:19Z","intro":"Ennis Rakestraw Jr. (born June 5, 2002) is an American professional football cornerback for the Detroit Lions of the National Football League (NFL). He played college football for the Missouri Tigers. Rakestraw was selected by the Lions in the second round of the 2024 NFL draft.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Rakestraw Jr. was born in Dallas, Texas, and attended Duncanville High School in Duncanville, Texas. As a senior in 2019, he was named the SportsDayHS Defensive Player of the Year by the Dallas Morning News. He committed to University of Missouri to play college football."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"As a freshman at Missouri in 2020, Rakestraw started all 10 games and had 24 tackles and one sack. As a sophomore in 2021, he played in four games before suffering a torn ACL which ended his season. He returned from the injury to start all 13 games in 2022, finishing the season with 35 tackles and one interception. He returned to Missouri in 2023, finishing with 35 tackles, four passes defended and a forced fumble in nine games. Following the season he declared for the 2024 NFL draft."},{"key":"career","title":"Professional career","text":"Rakestraw was selected by the Detroit Lions with the 61st pick in the second round of the 2024 NFL draft.\nOn August 7, 2025, Rakestraw was placed on injured reserve after it was announced he would require shoulder surgery, ending his 2025 NFL season."}],"social":{}},"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4566092","pfr":"https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/R/RakeEn00.htm","pff":"https://www.pff.com/nfl/players/ennis-rakestraw-jr/124215","otc":"https://overthecap.com/player/ennis-rakestraw-jr/11669","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ennis_Rakestraw_Jr."},"insights":["On the field for 21% of Detroit’s defensive snaps this season.","2026 cap number of $1.8M is the 23rd-largest on the roster.","Under contract through 2027.","Drafted 61st overall in 2024 (round 2) by DET."]}